# Who the messages archive may send to, one `network target` per line.
#
# Copy this to `archive-send.allow` beside it and fill it in. The real file is
# NOT in this repository and must not be: xinutec/pippijn is public, and who
# Pippijn talks to is not something it should record. The example is here for
# the format only.
#
# ⚠ FAIL-CLOSED. A missing, unreadable or empty file refuses everything — the
# plugin treats "cannot read the list" as "nobody is on it". So the send path
# is inert until this file exists, which is the right state for it to be in
# after a fresh volume.
#
# `network` is irssi's server TAG, exactly as `/server list` shows it — not a
# hostname. `target` is a nick, or a channel including its leading `#`.
#
# Read fresh on every request, so adding a line takes effect immediately: no
# `/script load`, no restart, nothing to redeploy.
#
# Matching is case-insensitive on both fields, as IRC's own comparison is.
#
# A line whose first non-blank character is `#` is a comment. That is a
# whole-line rule rather than strip-to-end-of-line precisely because channel
# names begin with `#` — the obvious implementation deletes every channel entry
# and refuses them all, silently.

# examplenet somenick
# examplenet #somechannel
